com/users/mosche/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### CI Link\n\nhttps://gradle-enterprise.elastic.co/s/ssqi5r5klvhsm\n\n### Repro line\n\n./gradlew ':server:test' --tests \"org.elasticsearch.snapshots.SnapshotResiliencyTests*\" -Druntime.java=21  -Dtests.es.logger.level=DEBUG\n\n### Does it reproduce?\n\nYes\n\n### Applicable branches\n\nmain\n\n### Failure history\n\n_No response_\n\n### Failure excerpt\n\n```org.elasticsearch.snapshots.SnapshotResiliencyTests > testIllegalArgumentExceptionLogging FAILED\r\n    java.lang.AssertionError: expected to see INFO log but did not\r\n    Expected: <true>\r\n         but: was <false>\r\n        at __randomizedtesting.SeedInfo.seed([782F1BB9840950FE:32EBB1FE53CD0BB8]:0)\r\n        at org.hamcrest.MatcherAssert.assertThat(MatcherAssert.java:18)\r\n        at org.elasticsearch.test.MockLogAppender$SeenEventExpectation.assertMatched(MockLogAppender.java:127)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe following 4 tests started failing yesterday in `SnapshotResiliencyTests` due to an incorrectly set log-level.  \r\n```\r\nTests with failures:\r\n - org.elasticsearch.snapshots.SnapshotResiliencyTests.testIndexNotFoundExceptionLogging\r\n - org.elasticsearch.snapshots.SnapshotResiliencyTests.testFullSnapshotUnassignedShards\r\n - org.elasticsearch.snapshots.SnapshotResiliencyTests.testIllegalArgumentExceptionLogging\r\n - org.elasticsearch.snapshots.SnapshotResiliencyTests.testSnapshotNameAlreadyInUseExceptionLogging\r\n ```\r\n\r\n It seems that in this [PR](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/105020) we updated the log-level of the[ root logger](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/main/server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/common/logging/LoggersTests.java#L88) as part of the tests, so if it happens that the `SnapshotResiliencyTests` are executed **after** the `LoggersTests`, the log-level for the `SnapshotsService` logger will be set to debug causing the failures above.  \r\n\r\nWe should probably reset the log-level after the tests, as we do in `InternalEngineTests#testMergeThreadLogging`  for example","closed_by":{"login":"mosche","id":1401430,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDE0MzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1401430?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche","html_url":"https://github.com/mosche","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mosche/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/106250/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/106250/timeline","performed_via_github_